What are Parameters? (The Method's Blueprint) 📘

A parameter is a variable defined in the method's declaration. It acts as a named placeholder to receive data when the method is called. Think of parameters as the "ingredients required" on a recipe card—they specify what you need, but not the specific values.
In the following Java code, firstName and lastName are the parameters of the createFullName method. They define the type of data the method expects to receive.
public class User {

    // firstName and lastName are parameters
    public String createFullName(String firstName, String lastName) {
        return firstName + " " + lastName;
    }
}

